    "summary": "Saudi air defenses intercepted three ballistic missiles launched by Yemen's Houthi movement, one targeting Riyadh and two aimed at Khamis Mushait, marking a third consecutive day of such attacks.",
    "content": "Saudi Arabia's air defense forces intercepted three ballistic missiles fired by Yemen's Houthi movement on Tuesday, according to a statement from the Saudi-led coalition. Coalition spokesman Turki Al-Maliki said one missile was aimed at the capital, Riyadh, while the other two targeted the southwestern city of Khamis Mushait. All three were destroyed before reaching their targets, he said.\n\nThe interception marks the third consecutive day that Houthi forces have launched ballistic missiles into Saudi territory, according to coalition statements. The attacks come amid ongoing hostilities between the Iran-aligned Houthi movement and the Saudi-led coalition, which has been conducting airstrikes in Yemen since 2015 in support of the internationally recognized Yemeni government.\n\nKhamis Mushait, located near the border with Yemen, has frequently been a target of Houthi missile and drone attacks. Riyadh, the kingdom's political and economic center, has also been targeted in previous years, though such strikes on the capital are less common than those on border regions.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the continued escalation raises concerns about regional stability and potential disruptions to trade and travel routes. Many Somali communities in the Gulf, particularly in Saudi Arabia, rely on these corridors for remittances, business, and family connections. Prolonged conflict could affect the safety and economic security of those living in the region.\n\nThe Houthi movement has not commented on the latest attacks. The Saudi-led coalition has not reported any casualties or damage from the intercepted missiles. The situation remains tense as both sides continue military operations.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/13/xuutiyiinta-yemen-oo-maalintii-saddexaad-weerarro-gantaallo-ah-ku-beegsaday-caasimadda-sacuudiga-ee-riyadh/",
